{"name":"Echo Valley","hex":"#e6e2d6","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"echo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Echo of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reflected sound that is heard again by its initial observer.","An utterance repeating what has just been said."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/echo"},{"term":"valley","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elongated depression cast between hills or mountains, often with a river flowing through it.","An area which drains itself into a river."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form the shape of a valley."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Echo Valley (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Echo Valley is a 2025 American thriller film directed by Michael Pearce and written by Brad Ingelsby. The film stars Julianne Moore, Sydney Sweeney, Fiona Shaw, Kyle MacLachlan, and Domhnall Gleeson. Its plot follows a horse trainer who, while living a quiet life on a Pennsylvania farm, must aid her daughter who has come to her in an alarming state."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Echo_Valley_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echo_Valley_(film)","wikidata":"Q119053380"},{"title":"Echo","blocks":[{"text":"In audio signal processing and acoustics, an echo is a reflection of sound that arrives at the listener with a delay after the direct sound. The delay is directly proportional to the distance of the reflecting surface from the source and the listener. Typical examples are the echo produced by the bottom of a well, a building, or the walls of enclosed and empty rooms."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echo","wikidata":"Q182767"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Echo_Valley_poster.jpg/250px-Echo_Vall